    "findings": [],
    "summary": "ACCEPT. The reviewed correction is confined to test and artifact qualification. The historical demo profile contract requires a SHA-256 fingerprint of its canonical embedded bytes. Both reviewed JSON copies now have explicit LF checkout attributes; their worktree and Git bytes agree at b84223c2..., and the corrected fingerprint assertion matches. This protects accepted profile identity rather than an arbitrary source-text hash. The two newly grouped test classes each create and dispose owned PostgreSQL databases. Their shared disabled-parallelization collection follows an existing repository fixture pattern, addresses the observed parallel-suite timeouts, and leaves lifecycle assertions and exact cleanup intact. Serial diagnosis and the combined corrected boundary passed 27/27. All Story 18.1 production and PreparedSource test hashes match the earlier accepted quality boundary, preserving the resolutions of QR-18.1-01, QR-18.1-02, and QR-18.1-03. Convergence is clean, and lookback-05 and the project lesson describe the correction without claiming the pending configured full-suite rerun has passed. No new required finding was found. The focused checks do not qualify real Worker/model/provider integration or immutable Source Snapshot behavior; final full-suite verification remains required."
